Local fix (not upstream): restore the BAR1-P2P read cap that bridge discovery loses.

Measured on this host with everything else in place (64GB BAR1, static BAR1
enabled, all four kbusIsPcieBar1P2PMappingSupported_GH100 gates ACCEPTED):

  CMPUNLOCK_BAR1P2P: hostsys commonSwitch=0 cpuType=0x8 readCap=0x1 writeCap=0x0

readCap 0x1 is CHIPSET_NOT_SUPPORTED, which makes
_kp2pCapsGetStatusOverPcieBar1 return NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and the driver fall
back to the mailbox (connType=1). The read cap is granted only for a common
PCIe switch, Ryzen, or Xeon-SPR; this is a Xeon E5 v4, so it hinges on
bCommonPciSwitchFound -- and clFindCommonDownstreamBR() returns 0xFF here even
though lspci shows both GPUs on downstream ports of switch 09:00.0.

This restores the cap for CMP device IDs only. See the in-code note: it assumes
the cards really are behind a common switch, which must be re-verified on any
differently-wired machine.

--- m/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/p2p/p2p_caps.c	2026-08-07 18:24:45.256476055 -0700
+++ n/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/p2p/p2p_caps.c	2026-08-07 18:24:45.280088620 -0700
@@ -682,6 +682,37 @@
               (NvU32)bCommonPciSwitchFound, (NvU32)pSys->cpuInfo.type,
               (NvU32)*pP2PReadCapStatus, (NvU32)*pP2PWriteCapStatus);
 
+    //
+    // cmpunlocker P2P: the read cap above is granted only for a common PCIe
+    // switch, Ryzen, or Xeon-SPR. On this host (Xeon E5 v4) it depends entirely
+    // on bCommonPciSwitchFound, and clFindCommonDownstreamBR() fails to identify
+    // the PLX switch these cards sit behind -- it returns 0xFF even though lspci
+    // shows both GPUs on downstream ports of the same switch (09:00.0, common
+    // bus 0x0a). That false negative is the last thing forcing the mailbox path.
+    //
+    // Override it for CMP device IDs only. This is the same topology that is
+    // reported working elsewhere at ~1.4 GB/s, so the cap is being restored to
+    // what the hardware actually supports rather than invented.
+    //
+    // NOTE: this assumes the CMP GPUs really are behind a common switch. Verify
+    // with `lspci -tv` before trusting P2P on a differently-wired machine; if
+    // they are on separate root ports, peer traffic must cross the host bridge
+    // and this override would be wrong.
+    //
+    {
+        NvU32 cmpDevId = pGpu->idInfo.PCIDeviceID >> 16;
+
+        if (((cmpDevId == 0x20C2) || (cmpDevId == 0x2082)) &&
+            (*pP2PReadCapStatus != NV0000_P2P_CAPS_STATUS_OK))
+        {
+            NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
+                      "CMPUNLOCK_BAR1P2P: forcing read cap OK for CMP devId=0x%x "
+                      "(clFindCommonDownstreamBR did not detect the PLX switch)\n",
+                      cmpDevId);
+            *pP2PReadCapStatus = NV0000_P2P_CAPS_STATUS_OK;
+        }
+    }
+
     return NV_OK;
 }
 
